  "tagline": "Small Java NoSQL caching store built on relational internals (B+trees, block cache, JDBC); abandoned 2015.",
  "description": "WonderDB was a one-developer Java project by Vilas Athavale that applied relational database machinery (block caching, record-level locking, B+tree indexes, variable-size blocks, SQL and JDBC) to a disk-backed key-value cache. The published version exposed only get, put and remove against a local cache, with values in a disk-backed concurrent list, and the author reported around 33,000 operations per second for 1 KB payloads on an EC2 m3.xlarge. Development stopped in 2015 and the wonderdb.org domain is now parked. It is only of interest as a small code example.",
